{
	"_meta": {
		"schema": "db-ux/example/v1",
		"pageType": "process",
		"origin": "guideline-authored",
		"purpose": "Canonical PROCESS/wizard STEP frame (R=md reference): one step of a 4-step booking wizard. ONE narrow centered Section (contentWidth 'Small (768)') with the composed stepper on top (step 2 of 4 active, step 1 done), a step header (h1 + description), a form fieldset (the step's inputs), and a spread step-nav row (Zurück ghost + Weiter Brand). DENSITY/STYLE REFERENCE ONLY — a full wizard is rendered as SEPARATE step frames (one per step + a confirmation frame), never wired as a prototype.",
		"designNotes": "A process is delivered as a sequence of static step frames. Every step frame: progress indicator (current step highlighted) → step header → step content (a reused FORM fieldset) → step nav (Zurück left / Weiter right, spread). ONE Brand action per frame (Weiter/commit). The stepper is a guideline-authored composition (Badge markers + labels) — no Stepper component exists yet. Single canvas, no zebra.",
		"spacingModel": "A process inherits R from its product (content/website → lg, application/dashboard → md, dense data app → sm). This example is the R = md REFERENCE: elements in a block = md; grouped bits (step-header title↔desc, stepper marker↔label, fields) = sm/md; step-header → content = lg (R+1); progress/content/nav blocks = xl (R+2). Substitute per process/blocks.json → _meta.spacingModel.",
		"colorModel": "emphasis-100 for the step title + active step label; muted for the description, done/upcoming step labels. Stepper badges: done Successful, active Informational, upcoming Neutral."
	},
	"screen": "DB UX Process",
	"width": 1440,
	"variables": [
		"color.background.canvas",
		"color.text.strong",
		"color.text.muted"
	],
	"layout": [
